{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:25:54.389Z","ordinal":15700,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a02f71-5fd5-7ef0-aa50-14d1b6813bcf","author":"/root/phase2_integration_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/phase2_integration_audit\nPayload:\nRead-only audit complete. Focused suites pass:\n\n- `TestPackDistillCandidateMembersV2*`\n- `TestParseDistillCandidateMemberResultsV2*`\n- `TestDistillCandidateResultCacheV2*`\n- existing candidate pipeline/coalescing tests\n\nThe runtime is still Phase 1 plus Phase 2 scaffolding. `distill_packing_v2.go`, `distill_protocol_v2.go`, and `distill_cache_v2.go` are currently dead at execution time; only the v2 prompt is selected for `--shadow`.\n\nHighest-priority blockers:\n\n1. `--shadow` currently mutates manifest/taxonomy. In `runDistillForBrain`, `flushFactStoresLocked` returns early for shadow (`distill_cmd.go:1033`), but the final write block still calls `writeFactTaxonomy` and `updateBrainManifestAndReadme` (`distill_cmd.go:1348-1413`). It therefore changes taxonomy mtime/content handling, `sources.facts`, and README/manifest metadata. Add a shadow-only return before the final write block. If v2 cache persistence is intended, write only that cache under lock; never invoke the legacy flush or manifest writer.\n\n2. Shadow still executes the Phase 1 one-card path. `startSessionPrefetch` consumes `ps.chunks` (`distill_cmd.go:1131-1144`), and `packDistillCandidateCardsV1` deliberately emits one batch per card (`distill_candidates.go:1237-1295`). The v2 `CandidateBatches` field is preserved in preparation (`distill_cmd.go:2148-2225`) but never consumed.\n\n3. Shadow parses v2 output with the v1 parser. The loop calls `distilledFactsFromOutput` and then `candidateDistillOutputIsProtocolComplete` (`distill_cmd.go:1237-1253`). It must instead call `parseDistillCandidateMemberResultsV2`, map each member to its anchor, and apply taxonomy filtering/redaction/max-text checks before counting or caching facts.\n\n4. The v2 member cache is not loaded, looked up, populated, or saved anywhere in the runtime. The cache implementation is currently test-only. Add production identity construction for card/prompt/taxonomy/agent-command/model/effort/redaction, with confidence/branch/packing excluded as documented.\n\n5. Required pack accounting is absent. Add command-result-only counters for planned/succeeded/split/retried/failed/empty packs, member cache hits/misses, provider calls, and provider-reported usage. Existing `ExtractionCalls` alone cannot prove the Phase 2 operational gates.\n\nSmallest safe integration sequence:\n\n1. Keep `legacy` and non-shadow candidate v1 execution untouched.\n2. From the already complete-preflighted candidate snapshots, retain rendered card + anchor members and globally sort by session creation time, session ID, source turn, then candidate ID.\n3. Use `packDistillCandidateMembersV2` with the existing global concurrency pool. For each pack:\n   - look up each member independently;\n   - repack only misses;\n   - invoke the v2 prompt only for uncached members;\n   - parse atomically with `parseDistillCandidateMemberResultsV2`;\n   - on provider/protocol failure, bisect once into two halves;\n   - cache only protocol-valid member results, including explicit empty results.\n4. Consume completed packs in canonical source order, but do not materialize facts/proposals in shadow. Count ephemeral facts for the returned shadow summary.\n5. Persist v2 cache only if that is the intended contract. The task wording permits v2 cache mutation while requiring zero active facts, proposals, legacy cache, taxonomy, manifest, and README mutation; the current flag help says “cache” broadly and should be clarified.\n\nWithin-session packing is insufficient for the documented 30–60-call target. Current measured candidate mode is 368 calls because it sends one card per call. Packing only within candidate-bearing sessions bottoms out near the number of candidate sessions: the plan cites 57 for a narrower decision/learning projection, while the full candidate projection is 98 candidate sessions. Cross-session packing is required for a defensible 30–60 claim. The synthetic v2 packer test gives 368 cards / ~1.4 MB → 46 calls, which is consistent with the target, but this is not yet runtime evidence.\n\nQuality/privacy concerns to cover with integration tests:\n\n- shadow leaves facts, proposals, `facts/distill-cache.json`, taxonomy, manifest, and README byte-identical;\n- second shadow run uses v2 member cache and makes zero provider calls;\n- unknown/missing/duplicate candidate IDs never cache any member from that failed pack;\n- one malformed pack bisects once and accounts for all attempts;\n- cached empty results suppress future calls;\n- model/prompt/taxonomy changes invalidate extraction only; confidence changes do not;\n- facts are taxonomy-valid, redacted, bounded, and anchored to the member’s exact source span;\n- provider usage counts actual attempts, including failed and bisected calls, excluding cache hits.\n\nAgainst `docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md`: Phase 1 is substantially complete; Phase 2 has the data structures, prompt, parser, cache, and packer tests, but no runtime wiring, no member-level accounting, and currently violates the zero-mutation shadow contract."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4"}}}
