rieval\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:205:recall and can label the same assistant line as decision, learning,\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:684:- the rule has 100 percent precision on the retained supersession gold set.\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:827:baseline. Candidate bytes must never be relabeled as `preprocessed_bytes`.\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:946:metadata. Estimated tokens in dry run must be labeled estimates. Release\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:958:Build exact-span labels across:\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:987:Use at least two reviewers for ambiguous durable/known/resolved labels and\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:992:- At least 98 percent span recall for explicit human standing rules,\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:994:- At least 95 percent span recall across all gold durable facts.\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1001:  critical missed standing rule or closed negative. Any miss updates the gold\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1034:- Deterministic paraphrase merge precision is at least 99 percent on labeled\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1042:Run the existing facts evaluation arms on the resulting stores. Compare useful\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1044:must not claim a retrieval win unless proof-labeled paired evaluation supports\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1086:- Build the span-labeled gold and negative-audit sets.\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1089:meets the pre-agent gates on fixtures and the first gold slice.\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1117:- Compare outputs with legacy extraction and human labels.\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1119:Exit gate: candidate and fact-quality gates pass on the full labeled corpus;\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1147:- Make candidate mode the default only after all quality, retrieval,\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:117:> **Review: reinforcement classification has no existing foundation — this is the linchpin, see [Phase 0](#phase-0-reinforcement-classification-spike-prerequisite).** No code today labels a turn or checkpoint as `success` / `corrected` / `neutral`. Checkpoint metadata (`checkpointExportSession`) carries `Error`, `TokenUsage`, `Summary` but no outcome. Facts have a `Status` lifecycle (active/superseded/retracted), which is not a feedback signal. Yet reinforcement feeds the strength formula, the card header (\"12 success, 2 corrected\"), and the skill-memory `reinforcement` block. Do not treat \"classify basic reinforcement\" as a plumbing bullet — build and validate the rubric in Phase 0 first.\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:517:- **Fixtures + precision target:** `TestClassifyReinforcement` (25 labeled cases) and `TestReinforcementSignalsFromTranscript` (per-dialect extraction). Targets: accuracy ≥ 0.85, `corrected` precision ≥ 0.90, and **zero** approvals mislabeled as `corrected`. Current eval: accuracy 1.000, corrected precision 1.000, 0 violations.\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:518:- **Commit-success positive signal — DONE.** A second evidence source: the episode's work segment (turns between the request and the next request). A landed git commit — detected by its `[branch hash] subject` confirmation line, which git prints only on success and which appears literally in the raw transcript across dialects — labels the episode `success`, below user correction cues in precedence. This was added to recover the positive reinforcement that next-turn cues miss (see Phase 1 finding). `WorkCommitted` on `reinforcementSignal`; segmentation via `transcriptEpisodeSegments`.\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:526:- Apply the Phase 0 reinforcement classifier to label each episode (label is the classification of the *next* substantive user turn).\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:530:**Empirical finding (first real run, this repo's brain — 683 episodes):** the next-turn-only classifier came out **1 success / 10 corrected / 672 neutral**. The `corrected` labels are accurate on inspection (\"Try again\", \"Revert this…\", \"No, …\"), but positive reinforcement was nearly invisible to next-turn cues — on real CLI sessions users rarely type \"thanks/lgtm\"; they just issue the next request. **Resolution:** wiring the commit-success signal (above) lifted the same 683 episodes to **64 success / 10 corrected / 609 neutral** — spot-checked successes are genuine commit episodes (\"commit/push\", \"Commit the codex folder\"). `corrected` stays high-precision; `success` is now usable but skews toward commit-bearing episodes; `neutral` remains \"no signal\", not \"no value\". Strength scoring (Phase 2) can use `success` as a weak-positive but should not over-weight it.\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:541:- Render basic pattern cards. → concise read-only cards (strength label, command chain, support/branches, reinforcement tally, example anchor + id). The full evidence-first approval card lives in `patterns skills form` (Phase 5 redo).\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:648:2. Extract and persist `episodes.ndjson`, labeled by the Phase 0 classifier.\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:650:4. Add tests for episode extraction and reinforcement labels.\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:133:interpretation the future may not want, the way labeling a customer email a\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:142:is only ever a current best label over retained source that is still present. When\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:246:- `entire brain facts eval-gen [--refine] [--max-facts N]`, `facts eval\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:247:  [--judge] [--expand]`, and `facts eval-compare --a --b` — the retrieval\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:248:  evaluation harness: a provenance-labeled (optionally judge-refined) benchmark,\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:249:  per-stratum precision/recall/useful-per-1k metrics when proof labels or judge\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:250:  labels exist, source-match proxy metrics when explicitly allowed, and a paired\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:437:> benchmark. After growing the corpus to a provenance-labeled benchmark of **121\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:760:must be backed by paired `facts eval` evidence before public copy says facts are\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:783:  model is two keys plus a label: **WHERE** (code locus — a path/glob/package/\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:786:  as a roll-up label. Today's single taxonomy mashes where + kind + topic into\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:795:  label. Tie locus into the existing semantic index so \"changed files → relevant\ninternal/cli/episodes.go:25:// SCOPE NOTE: episodes carry identity, intent, the reinforcement label (via the\ninternal/cli/episodes.go:170:\t\t\tlabel := classifyReinforcement(reinforcementSignal{\ninternal/cli/episodes.go:175:\t\t\tswitch label {\ninternal/cli/episodes.go:195:\t\t\t\tReinforcement:   label,\ndocs/memory_lifecycle_plan.md:23:| Outcome signal | `internal/cli/episodes.go` | Episodes with reinforcement labels (Phase 0 classifier + commit-success signal), derived token-free from exported sessions during refresh. |\ndocs/memory_lifecycle_plan.md:41:{\"t\":\"outcome\",  \"fact\":\"<id>\", \"at\":\"...\", \"episode\":\"<episode id>\", \"label\":\"reinforced|neutral|contradicted|reverted\"}\ndocs/memory_lifecycle_plan.md:68:extractor already segments sessions and labels reinforcement. Add a join pass:\ndocs/memory_lifecycle_plan.md:70:attach the episode's label to those facts as `outcome` events:\ndocs/memory_lifecycle_plan.md:231:explodes, the outcome join is mislabeled — fix before enforcement.\ndocs/memory_lifecycle_plan.md:240:- `facts eval` gains a `--vitality` slice: does usefulness-weighted ranking\ndocs/memory_lifecycle_plan.md:241:  beat the current ranking on the labeled benchmark? Adoption of ranking\ndocs/seed_plan.md:507:  not every intermediate one, so matching that set would mislabel genuine\ndocs/diffless_review_seam.md:109:labels each comparison as proof-ready, promotable, audit-gapped, saturated, or incomplete;\ndocs/vitality_receipts.md:29:`facts eval`/`eval-gen` (a measurement harness — benchmark serves must not\ndocs/vitality_receipts.md:101:  `facts eval` paired-proof bar).\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:84:- `entire brain facts eval --retriever facts|history|query|raw-sessions` compares\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:90:  source-overlap proxies rather than proof labels.\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:97:  (`explicit_label`, `partial_explicit_label`, `mixed_explicit_source_match`,\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:99:  credit from labeled recall and spot query arms that mix fact labels with other\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:100:  source types. The human table now prints each row's relevance/label source and\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:106:  `evidence_basis` (`proof_labels`, `proxy_or_mixed`, `operational`, or\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:109:- `facts eval` validates `label_source`; task files with `relevant` ids must\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:110:  say whether labels are `human`, `judge_refined`, or `provenance_silver`.\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:113:  explicit, so same-id eval runs with different task labels or brain state\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:120:  `evidence_basis: \"proof_labels\"`. The audit also requires top-level\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:122:  required proof-label claim where the `facts` arm beats `raw-sessions`, so a\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:131:  complete proof-labeled facts-over-raw comparison with\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:149:explicit-label recall, `source_match` proxy credit, provenance-silver labels, or\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:154:with `facts eval-gen --source sessions --limit 8` had\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:159:rounded deliberately; re-run locally rather than citing these digits); `query` had no relevance labels for\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:164:Blocked evidence collection: paired `facts eval` runs for `facts`, `history`,\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:165:`query`, and `raw-sessions` over the same proof-labeled task set are still\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:172:1. Build a task file with `facts eval-gen --source sessions --out\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:174:   `relevant` ids with human or judge-refined labels and `label_source:\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:177:   `facts eval --tasks /tmp/entire-facts-eval-tasks.json --retriever facts\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:180:3. Compare pairs with `facts eval-compare --a /tmp/raw.json --b /tmp/facts.json\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:182:   release claims require `evidence_basis: \"proof_labels\"` and\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:403:  relevance credit without claiming recall labels they do not have.\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:404:- Eval result JSON now includes `relevance_source`, making explicit labels,\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:405:  source-match proxy credit, judge credit, and no-label tasks distinguishable.\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:407:  unless `--allow-proxy-comparison` is passed, so proxy-vs-label and\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:411:  label files or changed brain state cannot produce quiet significance claims.\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:421:- `facts eval --help` now shows `label_source` alongside `relevant` labels, so\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:422:  the copied example matches the loader's proof-label validation rules.\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:680:- Paired `entire brain facts eval --retriever facts|history|query|raw-sessions`\ndocs/release_readiness_audit.md:681:  runs over the same proof-labeled task set, same task hash, and same brain\ndocs/release_press_release.md:93:- Facts-vs-session retrieval quality, using paired `facts eval --retriever`\ndocs/release_press_release.md:94:  comparisons over shared proof labels. Proxy-comparison opt-in remains\ndocs/release_press_release.md:95:  smoke and calibration only and must be labeled as such. Facts ship as a\ndocs/release_press_release.md:115:- Frontend/hosted-model distill latency, paired facts evals, and broader\ndocs/release_press_release.md:165:  paired facts evals with active durable facts and proof labels, and\ndocs/pattern_v2.md:387:  strength_label TEXT NOT NULL,\ndocs/pattern_v2.md:644:outcome_score     = 0.5 when no labeled outcome, otherwise\ndocs/pattern_v2.md:668:Strength labels:\ndocs/pattern_v2.md:1060:**Next slices (this branch):** richer evidence (`episode_files`, `meta_hits` classifier, fact/symbol/commit links), synapses, the corpus-driven multi-family candidate/scoring layer (replacing the flat-file discovery as the analytical source), consolidation dossiers, then surface integration and product eval — each proven against the existing brain before it joins default retrieval.\ndocs/pattern_v2.md:1100:- **No public eval command** was added: a precision/noise-rate eval would need labeled fixtures and is not yet warranted; the plan permits a documented eval command but prefers tests first, and adding a hidden one is forbidden. The drift sub-states (current/update/edited/missing/reconsider/declined) already live in skill-memory; corpus dossiers carry `current`/`stale`.\ndocs/pattern_v2.md:1147:Themes are no longer grouped by `intent_sig` at refresh. Refresh stays token-free (it only classifies `episode_shapes`). The explicit, egress-gated `patterns verify --themes` samples recent read-only/conversation episodes (capped, redacted intent+excerpt) and asks an agent to group them into coherent latent practices BY MEANING — so differently-worded episodes about the same practice cohere, while same-`intent_sig` episodes about unrelated topics do not. The agent curates membership and assigns a verdict (it can drop members / mark `needs_split`); each accepted seed is then deterministically expanded by intent overlap, fingerprinted, and stored. Cached by the sample fingerprint (unchanged sample → no re-spend). Theme records carry the agent's description (not an intent label), and theme→skill flows through that verified record. Validated by the SR4 tests above.\ndocs/getting-started.md:648:entire brain facts eval-gen > facts-tasks.json\ndocs/getting-started.md:649:entire brain facts eval --tasks facts-tasks.json --retriever facts --json > facts-eval.json\ndocs/getting-started.md:650:entire brain facts eval-compare --a <before.json> --b <after.json>\ndocs/brain_brief_profiling.md:57:only. Those order labels make no OS-cache cold/warm claim, and the resulting\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:17:Before any change, the current `facts eval` numbers over the live `entire-brain`\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:18:`main` corpus (930 facts @ `3391f76`, **17** deterministic provenance-labeled\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:19:tasks from `facts eval-gen --branch main`, k=10). Every later stage compares\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:31:two-bucket problem Part B attacks. Repro: `facts eval-gen --branch main` then\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:32:`facts eval --tasks <f> --branch main --k 10 --json` (± `--semantic`),\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:50:detect from a path/keyword prior, so the agent-labeled path (distill prompt) is\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:67:deliberate — it stops an inference-fallback from clobbering an agent label across\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:68:runs — but it means agent re-labels are not automatically picked up.\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:70:Gotcha-labeling quality on the existing corpus is **deferred to a post-B4 call**\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:71:(the eval decides whether kind labels lift retrieval before we invest in agent\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:124:`facts eval --arm flat|scoped|outline` selects the retrieval structure\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:180:- The gotcha-labeling question (deferred post-B4) can stay deferred: the *win came\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:181:  from locus scoping, not kind* — kind labels did not drive the result — so better\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:182:  gotcha labels are not on the critical path to the measured gain.\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:185:`facts eval --tasks <f> --branch main --k 10 --arm {flat,scoped,outline} --json`;\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:207:- **Evaluation harness:** `facts eval-gen` (provenance-labeled benchmark from the\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:208:  brain's own sessions), `facts eval` (precision / recall / **useful-per-1k**),\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:209:  `facts eval-compare` (paired t-test via regularized incomplete beta, verified\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:214:Benchmark: **121 provenance-labeled tasks across 3 repos** — entire-brain (8),\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:262:   int8-quantized table, golden-parity tested against reference vectors.\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:284:   `facts eval --retriever ...` harness and commit sanitized summaries before\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:353:# regenerate a benchmark (recall-oriented labels; add --refine for precision-clean)\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:354:/tmp/eb-test facts eval-gen --out /tmp/cli_raw.json\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:356:# score it (deterministic with provenance labels)\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:357:/tmp/eb-test facts eval --tasks /tmp/cli_raw.json --json --k 10\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:360:/tmp/eb-test facts eval-compare --a base.json --b variant.json\ndocs/durable_facts_handover.md:391:  (Appendix C/D) — a labeling/ingestion-quality follow-up, independent of\ndocs/brain_wire_contract.md:283:Binding the metadata means a valid signature cannot be **relabeled** under a\ndocs/brain_wire_contract.md:476:- **Wrong key** — a different key gives `ErrKeyMismatch`; an envelope relabeled\ndocs/ga-readiness.md:16:| 5 | No-egress + deterministic golden coverage | ✅ exists | `doctor` `no_egress:true`; golden/provider/quality tests green (GA acceptance bar) |\ndocs/eval_ledger.md:11:| 2026-06-08 | entire-brain `main`, 179 facts, 16 provenance-labeled tasks (`facts eval-gen`, k=10) | lexical-only vs Model2Vec fused | lexical 0.86 → fused **1.50 useful/1k** (+76%); concept stratum 0 → 0.79 | Frozen Stage 0 baseline; any later embedder swap must beat 1.50 on this set. Also: facts FTS5 BM25 measured at parity (1.43), so BM25 ships **opt-in** (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_FACTS_BM25=1`), not default | `../alignment.md` (Stage 0); artifacts at `<brain>/eval/baseline-20260608/` |\ndocs/eval_ledger.md:18:| 2026-06-10 | entire-brain live brain, **history layer**: 33.8k rankable records, 13 provenance-labeled tasks (`history-eval-gen`, k=10) | substring vs BM25 vs Model2Vec-fused (`history-eval` arms) | substring 0.315 → **BM25 0.927 useful/1k (2.9×)**, precision 0.062 → 0.146 — first quantitative confirmation of the shipped BM25 default. Cutoff sweep 0.15/0.30/0.50: **within noise** → the shipped 0.30 stands. Fused (Model2Vec) 1.219 (+31% over BM25), 4W/3L/6T — **directional only**: n=13 with 6 all-zero tasks leaves 7 informative pairs, far from significant. Tension with the 2026-06-08 \"M2V noise on history\" probe is real but explainable: that probe measured raw cosine separation on paraphrases; RRF fusion bounds how much a weak semantic arm can hurt while letting its agreements help | History eval harness landed (`history-eval-gen` / `history-eval`); cutoff question **closed**; history semantic arm **stays unshipped** pending an EmbeddingGemma run (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_EMBEDDER=ollama … --arm fused`) and a second repo | this repo (`internal/cli/history_eval.go`); task set regenerable via `history-eval-gen` |\ninternal/cli/add_test.go:72:\t// history/doc hits carry a real file path; fact hits carry taxonomy labels.\ninternal/cli/add_test.go:79:\t\tt.Errorf(\"fact result must have no open target (Path is a taxonomy label), got %q\", fact.OpenPath)\ndocs/archive/progress-so-far.md:574:    labels for decisions, validation, tool paths, architecture, and sessions;\ndocs/archive/progress-so-far.md:658:- Facts-vs-session claims remain pending until paired `facts eval --retriever\ndocs/archive/progress-so-f