ompare_test.go.fixture\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/fixtures/validation/entireio-cli/flush_probe_window_hidden_test.go.fixture\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/fixtures/validation/entireio-cli/finalize_redaction_hidden_test.go.fixture\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/confirmatory/test_offline_relevance_eval.py\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/facts-eval-audit-report.md\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/facts-eval-audit-report.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/manifest.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/facts-status.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval/README.md\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/fixtures/task-validity/oracle-assisted-regressions.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval-proof-fixture/raw-vs-facts.compare.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval-proof-fixture/facts.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval-proof-fixture/facts-eval-audit-report.md\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval-proof-fixture/facts-eval-audit-report.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval-proof-fixture/manifest.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval-proof-fixture/README.md\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval-proof-fixture/history.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval-proof-fixture/query.json\nbenchmarks/agent-brain/evidence/facts-eval-proof-fixture/raw-sessions.json\n"},"started_at_ms":1787502948840,"completed_at_ms":1787502948840}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:35:48.902Z","ordinal":15943,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a02f7a-7226-7a40-8a2b-6f361b8ad3bb","call_id":"call_VnlePj3ew6E5Fb2Ku8k0s2x6","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"docs/release-blockers.md:63:**R1 — Eval label discipline orphaned the history-eval pipeline** (fixed in\ndocs/release-blockers.md:66:output. Fix separates ground-*truth* (same explicit labels, same source →\ninternal/cli/semantic_test.go:2654:\tassertTrust := func(label, output string) {\ninternal/cli/semantic_test.go:2657:\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s JSON missing trust diagnostics:\\n%s\", label, output)\ninternal/cli/semantic_test.go:2660:\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s JSON missing language_tiers:\\n%s\", label, output)\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:147:  recall across all human-labeled durable facts before the agent runs.\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:204:not themselves durable-fact candidates. History deliberately favors retrieval\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:205:recall and can label the same assistant line as decision, learning,\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:684:- the rule has 100 percent precision on the retained supersession gold set.\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:827:baseline. Candidate bytes must never be relabeled as `preprocessed_bytes`.\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:946:metadata. Estimated tokens in dry run must be labeled estimates. Release\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:958:Build exact-span labels across:\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:987:Use at least two reviewers for ambiguous durable/known/resolved labels and\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:992:- At least 98 percent span recall for explicit human standing rules,\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:994:- At least 95 percent span recall across all gold durable facts.\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1001:  critical missed standing rule or closed negative. Any miss updates the gold\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1034:- Deterministic paraphrase merge precision is at least 99 percent on labeled\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1042:Run the existing facts evaluation arms on the resulting stores. Compare useful\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1044:must not claim a retrieval win unless proof-labeled paired evaluation supports\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1086:- Build the span-labeled gold and negative-audit sets.\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1089:meets the pre-agent gates on fixtures and the first gold slice.\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1117:- Compare outputs with legacy extraction and human labels.\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1119:Exit gate: candidate and fact-quality gates pass on the full labeled corpus;\ndocs/candidate_distillation_plan.md:1147:- Make candidate mode the default only after all quality, retrieval,\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:117:> **Review: reinforcement classification has no existing foundation — this is the linchpin, see [Phase 0](#phase-0-reinforcement-classification-spike-prerequisite).** No code today labels a turn or checkpoint as `success` / `corrected` / `neutral`. Checkpoint metadata (`checkpointExportSession`) carries `Error`, `TokenUsage`, `Summary` but no outcome. Facts have a `Status` lifecycle (active/superseded/retracted), which is not a feedback signal. Yet reinforcement feeds the strength formula, the card header (\"12 success, 2 corrected\"), and the skill-memory `reinforcement` block. Do not treat \"classify basic reinforcement\" as a plumbing bullet — build and validate the rubric in Phase 0 first.\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:517:- **Fixtures + precision target:** `TestClassifyReinforcement` (25 labeled cases) and `TestReinforcementSignalsFromTranscript` (per-dialect extraction). Targets: accuracy ≥ 0.85, `corrected` precision ≥ 0.90, and **zero** approvals mislabeled as `corrected`. Current eval: accuracy 1.000, corrected precision 1.000, 0 violations.\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:518:- **Commit-success positive signal — DONE.** A second evidence source: the episode's work segment (turns between the request and the next request). A landed git commit — detected by its `[branch hash] subject` confirmation line, which git prints only on success and which appears literally in the raw transcript across dialects — labels the episode `success`, below user correction cues in precedence. This was added to recover the positive reinforcement that next-turn cues miss (see Phase 1 finding). `WorkCommitted` on `reinforcementSignal`; segmentation via `transcriptEpisodeSegments`.\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:526:- Apply the Phase 0 reinforcement classifier to label each episode (label is the classification of the *next* substantive user turn).\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:530:**Empirical finding (first real run, this repo's brain — 683 episodes):** the next-turn-only classifier came out **1 success / 10 corrected / 672 neutral**. The `corrected` labels are accurate on inspection (\"Try again\", \"Revert this…\", \"No, …\"), but positive reinforcement was nearly invisible to next-turn cues — on real CLI sessions users rarely type \"thanks/lgtm\"; they just issue the next request. **Resolution:** wiring the commit-success signal (above) lifted the same 683 episodes to **64 success / 10 corrected / 609 neutral** — spot-checked successes are genuine commit episodes (\"commit/push\", \"Commit the codex folder\"). `corrected` stays high-precision; `success` is now usable but skews toward commit-bearing episodes; `neutral` remains \"no signal\", not \"no value\". Strength scoring (Phase 2) can use `success` as a weak-positive but should not over-weight it.\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:541:- Render basic pattern cards. → concise read-only cards (strength label, command chain, support/branches, reinforcement tally, example anchor + id). The full evidence-first approval card lives in `patterns skills form` (Phase 5 redo).\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:648:2. Extract and persist `episodes.ndjson`, labeled by the Phase 0 classifier.\ndocs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md:650:4. Add tests for episode extraction and reinforcement labels.\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:133:interpretation the future may not want, the way labeling a customer email a\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:142:is only ever a current best label over retained source that is still present. When\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:246:- `entire brain facts eval-gen [--refine] [--max-facts N]`, `facts eval\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:247:  [--judge] [--expand]`, and `facts eval-compare --a --b` — the retrieval\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:248:  evaluation harness: a provenance-labeled (optionally judge-refined) benchmark,\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:249:  per-stratum precision/recall/useful-per-1k metrics when proof labels or judge\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:250:  labels exist, source-match proxy metrics when explicitly allowed, and a paired\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:437:> benchmark. After growing the corpus to a provenance-labeled benchmark of **121\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:760:must be backed by paired `facts eval` evidence before public copy says facts are\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:783:  model is two keys plus a label: **WHERE** (code locus — a path/glob/package/\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:786:  as a roll-up label. Today's single taxonomy mashes where + kind + topic into\ndocs/durable_facts_plan.md:795:  label. Tie locus into the existing semantic index so \"changed files → relevant\ninternal/cli/episodes.go:25:// SCOPE NOTE: episodes carry identity, intent, the reinforcement label (via the\ninternal/cli/episodes.go:170:\t\t\tlabel := classifyReinforcement(reinforcementSignal{\ninternal/cli/episodes.go:175:\t\t\tswitch label {\ninternal/cli/episodes.go:195:\t\t\t\tReinforcement:   label,\ndocs/memory_lifecycle_plan.md:23:| Outcome signal | `internal/