{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:40:50.056Z","ordinal":16096,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a0200a-63d8-7b21-adef-c3850aecebf7","turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-41705d01-7e89-40c3-a732-c669600e4362","process_id":"8514","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n \"Phase 2|assistant|corrobor|candidate ID|32|packing|relocation|token|quality gate|exit gate\" docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md | head -220 && sed -n '940,1070p' internal/cli/distill_candidates.go && sed -n '1,110p' internal/cli/distill.go && rg -n \"max.*output|256|output cap|distill.*Max\" internal/cli/distill*.go | head -100"],"cwd":"file:///Users/thomi/Projects/entire-brain","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'Phase 2|assistant|corrobor|candidate ID|32|packing|relocation|token|quality gate|exit gate' docs/candidate_distillation_plan.md","query":"Phase 2|assistant|corrobor|candidate ID|32|packing|relocation|token|quality gate|exit gate","path":"candidate_distillation_plan.md"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '940,1070p' internal/cli/distill_candidates.go","name":"distill_candidates.go","path":"internal/cli/distill_candidates.go"},{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,110p' internal/cli/distill.go","name":"distill.go","path":"internal/cli/distill.go"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'max.*output|256|output cap|distill.*Max' 'internal/cli/distill*.go'","query":"max.*output|256|output cap|distill.*Max","path":"distill*.go"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"11:cross-session packing, repository-evidence corroboration, and default rollout\n30:filtering works, not that the latency goal is met: candidate-id-framed packing\n66:but every remaining user and assistant line is still sent to a fact agent in\n73:cannot distinguish a human standing rule from an assistant's tentative review\n97:extraction call and one reconcile call, reported 7,179 provider tokens, and took\n115:| Same exchange set, excluding `agent_review` assistant claims | 815 exchanges | 1,576,942 | 57 normal-session paths |\n120:these figures are an opportunity bound, not the promised token reduction.\n138:key and that assistant text cannot inherit human authority merely because it is\n148:- Preserve the existing silent quality gate: most candidate cards should still\n161:- Reduce input tokens by 85-95 percent and total agent calls by at least 90\n173:- Do not treat assistant review findings, plans, or status reports as human\n192:| Visible conversation parsing | `internal/cli/conversation.go` | Reuse its dialect routing, wrapper filtering, visible-assistant allow-list, exact exchange ranges, and source digest. |\n205:recall and can label the same assistant line as decision, learning,\n223:    Role          string // user | assistant | summary\n224:    Origin        string // direct_user | slash_args | assistant_narrative | compaction | injected\n225:    Authority     string // human | assistant_claim | context_only | rejected\n238:The turn id must be stable across transcript relocation and a branch replay.\n284:- `empty`: the quality gate emitted no fact for this candidate;\n288:Caching individual member results means a retry or a later packing policy does\n301:- Claude Code `user` and `assistant` records;\n305:Only visible user and assistant narrative is eligible text. Thinking,\n333:  let the quality gate reject it; do not assign human authority by default.\n337:### Canonical assistant turns\n339:Assistant narrative is always an `assistant_claim`, never a repository fact by\n364:asking the quality gate,\" not \"write a fact.\"\n368:Triggers should be token-aware and boundary-aware rather than raw substring\n375:| Resolved decision | `decided`, `chose`, `agreed`, `instead of`, `rationale`, `tradeoff`, choice plus `because` | medium; requires resolution evidence for assistant text |\n378:| Gotcha or discovery | `root cause`, `turns out`, `only when`, `unless`, `otherwise`, `silent`, `hang`, `race`, `stale` | medium; assistant claims require corroboration |\n384:resolution, and corroboration.\n401:- an assistant plan that has not executed;\n427:| `agent_review` assistant claim without later acceptance/fix | -8 |\n439:Build the smallest window that lets the quality gate judge resolution and\n442:- For a user trigger, include that user turn and its following assistant\n444:- For an assistant trigger, include the preceding user request, the triggering\n445:  assistant span, and the next user acceptance, correction, or rejection.\n446:- For an explicit user acceptance, include the immediately preceding assistant\n473:assistant can accurately discover a gotcha, but the claim needs evidence before\n479:highest authority prior. They still pass the durable-fact quality gate for\n489:An assistant claim is eligible only when at least one corroboration route is\n521:second transcript. Commit bodies and summaries are corroboration or\n543:- Pack 8-32 cards while keeping rendered input at or below 16-32 KiB.\n545:  cross-session packing because every card carries complete identity.\n561:facts are also persisted per candidate member. This makes repacking,\n569:packing should reduce that further to approximately 30-60 extraction calls.\n589:| Redacted extraction | candidate-card digest after redaction, extraction-prompt version, taxonomy digest, agent command identity, model, effort | branch, transcript path, confidence threshold, packing policy | empty or parsed fact lines per candidate |\n590:| Reconciliation | reconciliation-rule version, candidate fact ids, active-neighbor identity | model, effort, packing policy | deterministic action or proposal identity |\n606:   complete the previous assistant candidate.\n654:- at least one strong locus or identifier token in common; and\n666:- token-shingle or weighted-Jaccard similarity above a measured threshold;\n679:- the newer source has direct human authority or an accepted assistant claim;\n808:    \"assistant_corroborated\": 803,\n809:    \"assistant_suppressed\": 41\n839:- per-stage wall time and existing provider token usage.\n934:- assistant claims corroborated, suppressed, and review-gated;\n937:- extraction calls, token usage, wait time, and facts emitted;\n945:Provider token accounting remains provider-reported and keeps completeness\n946:metadata. Estimated tokens in dry run must be labeled estimates. Release\n965:- assistant discoveries later accepted or implemented;\n966:- rejected, corrected, and unresolved assistant claims;\n981:- authority and required corroboration;\n1006:quality gate offline during evaluation. Review any fact it emits that candidate\n1010:### Fact-quality gates\n1020:- human-authority and corroboration correctness;\n1026:- facts emitted per 1,000 input tokens.\n1043:facts per 1,000 tokens, precision, recall, and answer support. Candidate mode\n1063:- at least 85 percent fewer provider input tokens;\n1068:- transcript relocation and branch replay make zero extraction calls;\n1110:### Phase 2: Candidate-pack extraction, shadow only\n1119:Exit gate: candidate and fact-quality gates pass on the full labeled corpus;\n1120:token/call accounting is complete.\n1163:7. Add deterministic packing, member cache, split retry, and concurrency tests.\n1176:- content-address stability across path, branch, checkpoint, packing, and\n1194:- Human and assistant text carry different authority.\n1208:- Does one pack per candidate-bearing session outperform cross-session packing\n1217:  without erasing the measured token reduction?\n}\n\nvar distillCandidateQuestionV1 = regexp.MustCompile(`(?i)^(?:should|must|can|could|would|do|does|did|is|are|what|how|why|when)\\b.*\\?\\s*$`)\nvar distillCandidateStrongQuestionDirectiveV1 = regexp.MustCompile(`(?i)\\b(?:always|never|make sure|from now on|going forward|whenever|every time)\\b`)\nvar distillCandidateAdjacentAcceptanceV1 = regexp.MustCompile(`(?i)^(?:yes|correct|that works|go ahead|do that)[.!]?\\s*$`)\nvar distillCandidateOneOffWantV1 = regexp.MustCompile(`(?i)\\bi want\\s+(?:you\\s+)?to\\b`)\n\nfunc distillCandidateCuesV1(text string) []distillCandidateCueV1 {\n\ttrimmed := strings.TrimSpace(text)\n\tif distillCandidateQuestionV1.MatchString(trimmed) && !distillCandidateStrongQuestionDirectiveV1.MatchString(trimmed) {\n\t\treturn nil\n\t}\n\tvar cues []distillCandidateCueV1\n\tfor _, rule := range distillCandidateCueRulesV1 {\n\t\tif rule.Pattern.MatchString(text) {\n\t\t\tif rule.Cue == distillCandidateCuePreferenceV1 && distillCandidateOneOffWantV1.MatchString(text) &&\n\t\t\t\t!strings.Contains(strings.ToLower(text), \" instead of \") && !strings.Contains(strings.ToLower(text), \" rather than \") {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tcues = append(cues, rule.Cue)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn cues\n}\n\n// selectDistillCandidateCardsV1 creates one bounded context card per\n// cue-bearing user turn. Assistant text is context, never direct authority; an\n// accepted assistant proposal is admitted by the following user's explicit\n// acceptance cue. Keeping cards independent prevents a cue-dense transcript\n// from transitively becoming one provider-sized mega-card.\nfunc selectDistillCandidateCardsV1(transcript distillNormalizedTranscriptV1) []distillCandidateCardV1 {\n\tcards, _ := selectDistillCandidateCardsLimitedV1(transcript, 0)\n\treturn cards\n}\n\n// selectDistillCandidateCardsLimitedV1 stops during trigger discovery, before\n// card/window copies are allocated, when limit is exceeded. limit<=0 is\n// unbounded and is reserved for focused tests/local helpers; provider planning\n// always supplies the per-session admission cap.\nfunc selectDistillCandidateCardsLimitedV1(transcript distillNormalizedTranscriptV1, limit int) ([]distillCandidateCardV1, bool) {\n\ttype triggerAt struct {\n\t\tindex int\n\t\tcues  []distillCandidateCueV1\n\t}\n\tvar triggers []triggerAt\n\tfor index, turn := range transcript.Turns {\n\t\tif turn.Role != distillTranscriptRoleUserV1 || !turn.DirectUser {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tcues := distillCandidateCuesV1(turn.Text)\n\t\tif len(cues) == 0 && index > 0 && transcript.Turns[index-1].Role == distillTranscriptRoleAssistantV1 && distillCandidateAdjacentAcceptanceV1.MatchString(strings.TrimSpace(turn.Text)) {\n\t\t\tcues = []distillCandidateCueV1{distillCandidateCueAcceptanceV1}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif len(cues) > 0 {\n\t\t\ttriggers = append(triggers, triggerAt{index: index, cues: cues})\n\t\t\tif limit > 0 && len(triggers) > limit {\n\t\t\t\treturn nil, true\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif len(triggers) == 0 {\n\t\treturn nil, false\n\t}\n\n\tcards := make([]distillCandidateCardV1, 0, len(triggers))\n\tfor _, trigger := range triggers {\n\t\tstart, end := trigger.index, trigger.index\n\t\tif trigger.index > 0 && transcript.Turns[trigger.index-1].Role == distillTranscriptRoleAssistantV1 {\n\t\t\tstart--\n\t\t}\n\t\tif trigger.index+1 < len(transcript.Turns) && transcript.Turns[trigger.index+1].Role == distillTranscriptRoleAssistantV1 {\n\t\t\tend++\n\t\t}\n\t\tturns := append([]distillNormalizedTurnV1(nil), transcript.Turns[start:end+1]...)\n\t\tacceptance := distillCandidateCueSliceContainsV1(trigger.cues, distillCandidateCueAcceptanceV1)\n\t\tfor index := range turns {\n\t\t\tvar cues []distillCandidateCueV1\n\t\t\tif start+index == trigger.index {\n\t\t\t\tcues = trigger.cues\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tredacted := redactText(turns[index].Text)\n\t\t\tif start+index == trigger.index {\n\t\t\t\t// Never silently remove a second rule/qualifier from the same\n\t\t\t\t// authoritative turn. Packing shrinks adjacent context first and\n\t\t\t\t// refuses the card if this complete redacted trigger cannot fit.\n\t\t\t\tturns[index].Text = redacted\n\t\t\t} else if acceptance && turns[index].Role == distillTranscriptRoleAssistantV1 && start+index == trigger.index-1 {\n\t\t\t\tturns[index].Text = boundDistillCandidateTextHeadTailV1(redacted, distillCandidateTurnMaxRunes)\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\tturns[index].Text = boundDistillCandidateTextV1(redacted, cues, distillCandidateTurnMaxRunes)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\ttriggerTurn := transcript.Turns[trigger.index]\n\t\tcardTriggers := []distillCandidateTriggerV1{{\n\t\t\tTurnID:        triggerTurn.ID,\n\t\t\tRole:          triggerTurn.Role,\n\t\t\tCues:          append([]distillCandidateCueV1(nil), trigger.cues...),\n\t\t\tAuthoritative: true,\n\t\t}}\n\t\tstartLine, endLine := turns[0].StartLine, turns[0].EndLine\n\t\tidParts := []string{distillCandidateSourceIdentityV1(transcript.Source)}\n\t\tfor _, turn := range turns {\n\t\t\tstartLine = min(startLine, turn.StartLine)\n\t\t\tendLine = max(endLine, turn.EndLine)\n\t\t\tidParts = append(idParts, turn.ID)\n\t\t}\n\t\tfor _, trigger := range cardTriggers {\n\t\t\tidParts = append(idParts, trigger.TurnID)\n\t\t\tfor _, cue := range trigger.Cues {\n\t\t\t\tidParts = append(idParts, string(cue))\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tcards = append(cards, distillCandidateCardV1{\n\t\t\tSchemaVersion: distillCandidateSchemaVersion,\n\t\t\tID:            distillCandidateStableIDV1(\"candidate-v1:\", idParts...),\n\t\t\tSource:        transcript.Source,\n\t\t\tStartLine:     startLine,\n\t\t\tEndLine:       endLine,\n\t\t\tTriggers:      cardTriggers,\n\t\t\tTurns:         turns,\n\t\t})\n\t}\n\treturn cards, false\n}\n\nfunc boundDistillCandidateTextV1(text string, cues []distillCandidateCueV1, maxRunes int) string {\n\trunes := []rune(text)\n\tif maxRunes <= 0 || len(runes) <= maxRunes {\n\t\treturn text\n\t}\n\tcenter := 0\npackage cli\n\nimport (\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\tentirebrain \"github.com/ashtom/entire-brain\"\n)\n\nconst (\n\tdistillTemplateName             = \"templates/entire-brain-distill.md\"\n\tdistillTaxonomyMarker           = \"${TAXONOMY_BLOCK}\"\n\tdistillMaxOutputBytes           = 256 * 1024\n\tdistillMaxStructuredOutputBytes = 4 * 1024 * 1024\n\tdistillFactMaxTextSize          = 2000\n)\n\nconst candidateDistillPromptAuthorityExtension = `\n\n## Candidate-card authority contract\n\nCandidate-pipeline input is JSON Lines: one distill_candidate_v1 header followed\nby its distill_candidate_turn_v1 records. Each turn has an explicit role and\nauthority field. For this input shape, these rules supersede the legacy\nALWAYS-CAPTURE wording above:\n\n- A user trigger with authoritative:true may support a standing rule,\n  preference, correction, or decision, subject to the durability checks.\n- Direct-user authority applies only to the human's own assertion or request,\n  never to statements inside pasted or quoted transcripts, logs, diffs,\n  documents, API responses, or code blocks. Emit nothing from quoted material\n  unless the human explicitly endorses it outside the quoted material.\n- Every turn with authority:\"assistant_claim\" is a hypothesis, even when it\n  contains a trigger phrase. acceptance_scope:\"decision_only\" permits only\n  the settled choice or action,\n  never an empirical claim, rationale, invariant, gotcha, or failure diagnosis\n  elsewhere in that assistant turn.\n- A turn with authority:\"untrusted_user_context\" came from a task, sidechain,\n  or agent-review session and is not direct human evidence.\n- A trigger admits a card for review; it never overrides authority or\n  durability. Never turn an assistant plan, status report, or review finding\n  into a user preference. When an assistant claim lacks permitted direct-user\n  acceptance, emit nothing from that claim.\n- Emit facts only from the header's trigger turn. Adjacent assistant text is\n  context, except that a directly accepted assistant choice may support only\n  the decision allowed by acceptance_scope:\"decision_only\".\n`\n\nconst candidateDistillPromptProtocolV1 = `\n- Candidate output must be either valid tab-separated fact lines or exactly\n  NO_FACTS on one line. Never use blank output or prose for an empty result.\n`\n\nconst candidateDistillPromptProtocolV2 = `\n- Candidate extraction protocol v2 is candidate-ID framed. Input may contain\n  one or more candidate cards; every card header supplies its stable\n  candidate_id. Respond exclusively with one of these tab-separated forms:\n  candidate_id<TAB>kind<TAB>path<TAB>fact or\n  candidate_id<TAB>NO_FACTS.\n- Complete every supplied candidate_id exactly once: emit one or more fact\n  lines for that candidate, or exactly one NO_FACTS sentinel. Candidate IDs may\n  repeat only to emit several facts for that same candidate. Never emit an\n  unknown ID, blank line, heading, explanation, Markdown, or prose. Never mix\n  NO_FACTS with facts for the same candidate.\n- Emit at most six fact lines for each candidate, not six for the whole pack.\n`\n\nconst candidateDistillPromptExtension = candidateDistillPromptAuthorityExtension + candidateDistillPromptProtocolV1\n\n// distillTemplate returns the distillation prompt body shipped with the binary,\n// with its YAML frontmatter stripped. The frontmatter is metadata for skill\n// installers, not part of the prompt — and crucially the agent runners pass the\n// prompt as a positional CLI argument, so a leading \"---\" would be parsed as an\n// unknown flag and rejected. A missing template is a build error, not runtime.\nfunc distillTemplate() (string, error) {\n\tdata, err := entirebrain.Templates.ReadFile(distillTemplateName)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"read distill template: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn stripTemplateFrontmatter(string(data)), nil\n}\n\n// stripTemplateFrontmatter removes a leading YAML frontmatter block\n// (\"---\\n...\\n---\\n\") and returns the body. Content without frontmatter is\n// returned unchanged.\nfunc stripTemplateFrontmatter(content string) string {\n\tif !strings.HasPrefix(content, \"---\\n\") && !strings.HasPrefix(content, \"---\\r\\n\") {\n\t\treturn content\n\t}\n\tlines := strings.Split(content, \"\\n\")\n\tfor i := 1; i < len(lines); i++ {\n\t\tif strings.TrimSpace(lines[i]) == \"---\" {\n\t\t\t// Trim leading CR as well as LF: on Windows the template is checked out\n\t\t\t// with CRLF endings, so splitting on \"\\n\" leaves a stray \"\\r\" on the\n\t\t\t// blank line after the closing delimiter — trimming only \"\\n\" would\n\t\t\t// leave the body starting with \"\\r\\n\" (breaking the prefix the agent\n\t\t\t// runners expect and re-introducing a leading dash risk).\n\t\t\treturn strings.TrimLeft(strings.Join(lines[i+1:], \"\\n\"), \"\\r\\n\")\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn content // no closing delimiter; leave as-is\n}\n\n// renderDistillPrompt substitutes the active taxonomy into the template's\n// ${TAXONOMY_BLOCK} marker. The rendered prompt is what gets passed to the seed\n// agent as its system prompt; the line-numbered transcript chunk is the input.\nfunc renderDistillPrompt(taxonomy factTaxonomy) (string, error) {\ninternal/cli/distill_cache_v2_test.go:74:\t\t\"too large\":      []byte(strings.Repeat(\"x\", distillCandidateResultCacheV2MaxBytes+1)),\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:4:\t\"crypto/sha256\"\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:24:\t// existing six-fact output cap and one-anchor parser meaningful until a\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:27:\tdistillCandidateTurnMaxRunes        = 1536\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:28:\tdistillCandidateMaxCards            = 512\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:29:\tdistillCandidateMaxInputBytes       = 16 << 20\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:30:\tdistillCandidateMaxRawBytes         = 64 << 20\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:31:\tdistillCandidateMaxRecordBytes      = 2 << 20\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:32:\tdistillCandidateMaxMessageParts     = 4096\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:33:\tdistillCandidateMaxDocumentParts    = 32768\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:34:\tdistillCandidateMaxTurns            = 8192\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:35:\tdistillCandidateMaxTurnBytes        = 16 << 20\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:36:\tdistillCandidateMaxSourceFieldBytes = 8 << 10\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:40:\tdistillCandidateMaxPreflightBytes = 256 << 20\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:173:\tif len(sessionID) > distillCandidateMaxSourceFieldBytes ||\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:174:\t\tlen(checkpointID) > distillCandidateMaxSourceFieldBytes ||\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:175:\t\tlen(branch) > distillCandidateMaxSourceFieldBytes ||\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:176:\t\tlen(transcript) > distillCandidateMaxSourceFieldBytes {\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:185:\tif len(content) > distillCandidateMaxRawBytes {\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:196:\t\tif len(raw) >= distillCandidateMaxTurns || turnBytes > distillCandidateMaxTurnBytes {\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:242:\t\t\t\tif len(trimmed) > distillCandidateMaxRecordBytes {\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:250:\t\t\t\tif len(trimmed) <= distillCandidateMaxRecordBytes && !strings.HasPrefix(trimmed, \"{\") {\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:252:\t\t\t\t} else if len(trimmed) <= distillCandidateMaxRecordBytes {\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:475:\tnormalized.Grow(min(len(text), distillCandidateMaxRecordBytes))\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:1027:\t\t\t\tturns[index].Text = boundDistillCandidateTextHeadTailV1(redacted, distillCandidateTurnMaxRunes)\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:1029:\t\t\t\tturns[index].Text = boundDistillCandidateTextV1(redacted, cues, distillCandidateTurnMaxRunes)\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:1193:\tfor maxRunes := distillCandidateTurnMaxRunes; maxRunes >= 8; maxRunes /= 2 {\ninternal/cli/distill_candidates.go:1340:\tsum := sha256.Sum256([]byte(material))\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go:1061:\t\tdistillSessionCacheKeyForPipeline(distillPipelineCandidates, \"main\", \"s1\"): \"sha256:\" + strings.Repeat(\"a\", 64),\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go:1893:\t\tmainLegacy:       \"sha256:main-legacy\",\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go:1894:\t\tmainCandidate:    \"sha256:main-candidate\",\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go:1895:\t\tfeatureLegacy:    \"sha256:feature-legacy\",\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go:1896:\t\tfeatureCandidate: \"sha256:feature-candidate\",\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go:1897:\t\t\"s1\":             \"sha256:ambiguous-pre-upgrade\",\ninternal/cli/distill_shadow_v2_test.go:36:\tif err := saveDistillCache(brainDir, distillCache{Version: distillCacheVersion, Sessions: map[string]string{\"main/legacy\": \"sha256:legacy\"}}); err != nil {\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:6:\t\"crypto/sha256\"\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:75:\tsum := sha256.Sum256(data)\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:112:const distillSessionLookahead = 256\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:424:\t\t\tif totalCandidateBytes > distillCandidateMaxPreflightBytes {\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:425:\t\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"candidate preflight input exceeds %d bytes\", distillCandidateMaxPreflightBytes)\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:435:\t\treturn readCanonicalHistoryTranscriptBounded(ctx, brainDir, rel, int64(distillCandidateMaxRawBytes))\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:665:\tcmd.Flags().IntVar(&distillOpts.maxChunkBytes, \"max-chunk-bytes\", defaultDistillChunkSize, \"Maximum legacy transcript chunk or candidate-card input size in bytes\")\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1395:\t\tsource.MaxChunkBytes = distillMaxChunkBytes(distillOpts)\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1531:\t\tMaxChunkBytes:                 distillMaxChunkBytes(distillOpts),\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1557:\t\treport.MaxChunkBytes = distillCandidatePackMaxRenderedBytesV2\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1669:\t\t\t\treport.CandidatePacks, report.CandidatePacksIfUncached, distillCandidatePackMaxRenderedBytesV2, distillCandidatePackMaxMembersV2)\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1732:func distillMaxChunkBytes(distillOpts distillCommandOptions) int {\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1840:\t\tif pipeline == distillPipelineCandidates && plan.CandidateBytes > int64(distillCandidateMaxPreflightBytes) {\ninternal/cli/distill_cmd.go:1841:\t\t\treturn distillPlan{}, fmt.Errorf(\"candidate preflight input exceeds %d byte