{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:44:04.190Z","ordinal":16232,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a02f82-00de-7711-a807-9449bb8b1206","author":"/root/phase2_quality_gate","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/phase2_quality_gate\nPayload:\nSmallest safe implementation slice:\n\n1. Preserve the existing explicit-confirmation path as-is. A direct user acceptance creates a user-triggered card, and the renderer marks the preceding assistant turn `assistant_claim` with `acceptance_scope:\"decision_only\"`. Existing tests already prove this safely captures settled choices without promoting assistant rationale/gotchas.\n\n2. Add exactly one new assistant corroboration route: successful checkpoint + exact same-file mention.\n\n   Available evidence on `exportSession`:\n\n   - `Summary.Outcome`\n   - `FilesTouched`\n   - `Kind`, `IsTask`, `ToolUseID`, `LatestCheckpoint`, `CheckpointsCount`\n\n   Do not treat a non-empty checkpoint ID or `CheckpointsCount` as success. Add a strict allowlist helper for outcomes such as `success`, `succeeded`, `shipped`, `completed`, and `passed`; unknown/empty/in-progress/failed outcomes must not corroborate.\n\n   Require the assistant trigger text to contain an exact normalized full path from `FilesTouched` with path boundaries. Do not fall back to a basename or fuzzy symbol match in this slice. This makes the corroboration “successful checkpoint touching the same file,” rather than “any checkpoint.”\n\n3. Extend the in-memory normalized transcript/card contract with compact evidence booleans:\n\n```go\ntype distillCandidateEvidenceV1 struct {\n    CheckpointSuccess bool `json:\"checkpoint_success,omitempty\"`\n    SameLocus         bool `json:\"same_locus,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\nSet assistant triggers to:\n\n```go\nAuthoritative:          false\nCorroborationEligible:  true\n```\n\nRender the evidence in the candidate header, but do not copy the full `FilesTouched` list into provider input. Include the evidence feature digest in candidate ID material; changing checkpoint outcome or same-locus status must invalidate the member cache.\n\n4. Add assistant-trigger selection with these guards:\n\n- Eligible cues should be restricted to durable discovery/decision classes (`decision`, `closed_negative`, `gotcha`, `invariant`); exclude preference, acceptance, generic rule/status, and questions.\n- Skip `agent_review` claims unless the existing explicit user acceptance path applies.\n- Skip an assistant claim when the preceding user turn already has a direct-user candidate cue.\n- Skip an assistant claim when the next direct user turn explicitly accepts/corrects it; the existing user-triggered card is safer and already decision-scoped.\n- Otherwise build the plan-defined window: preceding substantive user turn, assistant trigger, and next substantive user turn when present.\n\nTests to add:\n\n- shipped checkpoint + exact touched path in assistant gotcha/decision → one assistant card, non-authoritative/corroboration-eligible, evidence rendered.\n- checkpoint present but empty/unknown/in-progress outcome → no assistant card.\n- successful checkpoint but no exact full-path mention → no assistant card.\n- basename-only mention → no card.\n- `agent_review` + checkpoint/files → no card without acceptance.\n- assistant status-only “implemented/fixed” → no card.\n- changing `Summary.Outcome` or `FilesTouched` changes/removes the candidate ID.\n- repeated normalization/planning remains byte-deterministic.\n- retain the current explicit-confirmation tests proving only the settled decision is eligible.\n\nWhat remains legitimately deferred:\n\n- Validation-record corroboration: `historyRecord` has `Kind`, transcript `Path`, `Line`, and summary, but the durable validation-to-session/checkpoint join is not currently a clean contract. Adding it is larger than this slice.\n- Independent recurrence: requires normalized claim equivalence across sessions and provenance-aware deduplication.\n- Symbol-locus corroboration through the entity index: possible, but introduces a separate derived-store join and ambiguity policy.\n- Human/model recall, precision, span faithfulness, and three-run provider comparisons remain Phase-2 exit evidence, not unit-test work.\n\nExplicit confirmation is therefore a safe, already-covered subset for assistant-origin decisions, but it does not close assistant-origin gotcha/discovery/closed-negative recall. The strict successful-checkpoint + exact-file route is the smallest implementation addition that closes one documented corroboration path without promoting every checkpoint."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4"}}}
