{"timestamp":"2026-08-23T16:50:34.704Z","ordinal":16422,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_0873a68aa02aff8f016a8b24d835a0819899bf397f16b7f086","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"The real-model smoke found the important truth the dry-run could not: the packed request fell back to one parent plus two isolated calls, and the local 7B model failed the v2 protocol on all three. It used 12,460 tokens and 161 seconds for zero accepted facts. I’m treating that as a failed quality/latency gate—not polishing the projection—and tracing the prompt/protocol conflict before deciding the smallest corrective step."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a02f65-7c17-7a30-9a2a-f255f8bc2ae4"}}}
